  "note": "One-time vol recalibration to an EQUAL structural wash target of 40% on every asset, effective 2026-07-26T06:00:00Z. Structural wash = P(the path never travels the band, either way, inside the horizon) \u2014 a property of price alone, measured on 90d of 1m bars. The board was not in fact vol-normalised: z = band/sigma_horizon was 0.94-1.06 on crypto but 0.57-0.59 on metals, so XAUUSD resolved ~4x more easily than BTCUSD and a gold call banked decisive outcomes a crypto call could not. The 2026-07-11 pass narrowed gold 88->62, which moved it further off curve, not onto it. Crypto is already on curve and barely moves; the correction is almost entirely metals. Signals committed before effective_from grade on the prior entry (no regrade). Maintained monthly from here by scripts/recalibrate_bands.py.",
