 {
  "version": "volnorm-equalwash40-tao165-20260811",
  "effective_from_unix": 1786417200,
  "note": "Adds TAOUSD (crypto) at 165 bps symmetric, effective 2026-08-11T03:00:00Z (pulled in from 2026-08-13T00:00:00Z on 2026-08-11 01:30Z, deliberately shortening validator lead time to ~1.5h \u2014 announce before the boundary), the first new pair since the 2026-07-21 FX expansion. Band solved with scripts/recalibrate_bands.py's own solve_band/excursions over its calendar-aligned 45d window (2026-06-26 -> 2026-08-10), LF target 40% structural wash, crypto horizon 8h: raw 165.40 -> 165, structural wash 39.74% on 4,170 samples, 45.0d of 45d coverage. Deadband and rate-limit do not apply to a new listing (both are defined against a current band and there isn't one). Grading substrate verified before listing: 100% of X:TAO-USD trades in a sampled hour landed on the graded venue allowlist (Coinbase 894, Kraken 361), so there is no Bittensor-thin-venue analogue of the Bitfinex drift that got venue 2 dropped. Tick density is thinner than the incumbent crypto pairs (allowlisted inter-tick p90 9.2s, max 131s vs sub-second on BTC), which matters for the two-tick touch rule; 165 bps is wide enough that this is not expected to bind. All 17 prior pairs are carried forward unchanged. HF deliberately NOT listed: Polygon serves no usable TAO top-of-book, so HF_TYPICAL_SPREAD_BPS cannot be measured on the graded substrate and band_spread_ratio returns None, which blocks the listing by design.",
  "bands": {
